  "title": "Debug NOR-Logic 8-to-3 Encoder",
  "description": "A student tried to build an 8-to-3 Octal-to-Binary encoder using only NOR gates to satisfy the lab constraint (No standard OR/AND gates allowed). However, the pre-wired circuit outputs incorrect binary codes when flipping switches I_4 through I_7. Inspect the NOR gate wiring, identify the missing connection or swapped input line, and fix it so that every active input produces its correct 3-bit binary code (A_2, A_1, A_0).\n\nConstraint: Strict Gate Restriction: The use of standard OR or AND gates is strictly prohibited. The circuit must be built using only NOR gates and Inverters.",
